Gardenbrooks:
A city of art everyone who lives there performs their art in one way or another, painters, dancers, singers, designers, they all co-exist in one town.
StarWhales show up every winter and bring the entire town together to touch and pat them as they head west, imagine sapenienza if it was constructed by rabid artists that's similar to what it looks like. 
[[Architecture]]
The town is centered around the preservation of culture and history protecting a Tree as old as time itself, art plastered everywhere, artists thriving, but forgetting the art old as themselves, sight that gets obscured by the emotion from strokes of paint splattered on the sidewalk, the art of being human. The art of justice, the art of crime, the art of sadisticness in its most prevalent form, exploring the cobblestone paths that lead to endless cafe's never struggling, people always doing, the sea side down with the docks, the art of fishing lives strong. Suspicious people lay in every interaction, as social anxiety, self confidence, and shyness live in the soul of almost everyone there. The sunsets rise and paint the sky golden rays of blood orange, the rain only fuels the city that never sleeps, that never dares to question what's above, their only aching question being that of creation. giant blimp sized whales fly over-head during the winter, holding peace within their beings, street lamps of old Victorian nature litter the streets, houses cramped together with style.
